_D_e_s_c_r_i_p_t_i_o_n:

     The ‘run_deseq2’ method of a ‘nexonsR’ object prepares counts and
     sample metadata, constructs a DESeq2 dataset, and runs
     ‘DESeq2::DESeq()’ with its default settings.

_U_s_a_g_e:

     x$run_deseq2(design, file = "gene", level = "gene", samples = NULL)
     
_A_r_g_u_m_e_n_t_s:

  design: The design passed to ‘DESeq2::DESeqDataSetFromMatrix’,
          usually a formula such as ‘~ condition’ or ‘~ batch +
          condition’. Variables refer to columns in the object's
          metadata. If supplying a model matrix, its rows must already
          correspond to the selected sample order.

    file: Exactly one of ‘"gene"’ (default), ‘"partial"’, or
          ‘"unique"’. The selected file must have been found at object
          creation.

   level: Exactly ‘"gene"’ (default) or ‘"isoform"’. Gene-level
          analysis of partial or unique tables sums counts by
          ‘Gene_ID’. Isoform analysis uses ‘Transcript_ID’ and requires
          partial or unique data.

 samples: Optional non-empty character vector of unique sample names.
          Both counts and metadata are selected and ordered by this
          vector. ‘NULL’ uses all samples in metadata order.

_D_e_t_a_i_l_s:

     Call this method on an object returned by ‘read_nexons()’. DESeq2
     is an optional dependency; install it using
     ‘BiocManager::install("DESeq2")’ before running the method. Only
     the selected table is lazily read and cached. Metadata is not
     modified. Unused factor levels are dropped from the selected
     metadata. Count columns and metadata rows are aligned by sample
     name.

     Counts must be finite, non-negative whole numbers and fit in R's
     integer range, including after aggregation. Counts are never
     rounded or normalized before fitting. Feature identifiers must be
     non-missing and non-empty; duplicates are allowed only when
     aggregating isoforms by gene. DESeq2 performs its own design and
     model checks and propagates fitting errors.

_V_a_l_u_e:

     A fitted ‘DESeqDataSet’, suitable for ‘DESeq2::results()’. The
     model is not stored in the nexonsR object.

_S_e_e _A_l_s_o:

     ‘read_nexons’

_E_x_a_m_p_l_e_s:

     ## Not run:
     
     x <- read_nexons("results")
     metadata <- x$get_metadata()
     # Supply annotations appropriate to your experiment:
     metadata$condition <- factor(c("control", "control", "treated", "treated"))
     x$set_metadata(metadata)
     model <- x$run_deseq2(~ condition)
     result <- DESeq2::results(model)
     isoform_model <- x$run_deseq2(~ condition, file = "unique", level = "isoform")
     ## End(Not run)
     

